                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wish there was a Neutral recommendation for games on steam. As I do not really recommend nor not recommend this game. It has it's own charms and is interesting to see a game with offering for two different VR headsets as well as a non-VR version. Something I wish all VR games would offer as I do not have a VR headset so missing out on quite a few of these games that look really awesome. I get that without VR some of these would be bad or simplistic to play but honestly I would find quite a few of them more entertaining if it offered a traditional movement system compared to VR system only.\n\nThis game in particular however does have some flaws in it for the non-VR version that I think overall I would have to say not recommend but the issues I have with the game may not be a problem at all for VR players.\n- Different Executables for Different VRs, ran into an issue where I ran the VR version because Steam stopped offering me a selection and it caused the game to run the VR version which caused other issues.\n- The Text for units and other descriptions in this game are extremely hard to read with camera placements on the non-VR version. Something that I believe may not be a problem in the VR version but it is hard to tell.\n- The camera movement for non-VR is absolutely garbage. Let me move the camera besides in-game settings!\n\nOther than those above that are VR related, I do have some issues with the gameplay itself:\n- Simplistic gameplay, non-unique gameplay. It gets really repitive. It almost feels like a demo than a full-fledged game. There is plenty of content though for it to be a game but the way the game handles overall isn't the most fun to me.\n- Not enough units. I feel like the unit selection between them all is a bit too low. I could honestly see many more units available for this game that would offer a bit more variation on strategy and combat.\n\nThere are some good things though, like the game does offer nice visuals for the environments and combat. The color scheme is easy to identify enemy projectiles and units and you can set-up yourself on the grid in any shape or pattern you want. This game would be great if it was a bit more flushed out in everything. As for now, I'll make this game as a recommended but overall I'm a bit neutral on the game itself.",
